#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""BackShot2 from the Mac (docs/design/backshot2.md, "Words"): runs bs2-host
on the test hosts over SSH, from a private copy of this worktree's testvm/
and holt/ in ~/backotter-work/bs2-wt (never the shared testvm/; BS2_WT=NAME-wt
names another, so two sessions' runs never share a copy).

  bs2 BackShot2Alpine [N] [plan]    N new cases (default 200) from each Alpine source,
                                    through tier 0, then tier 1, then tier 2 for the UEFI
                                    sources' cases that touch an ESP or the NVRAM (30 in all),
                                    then the corpus
  bs2 BackShot2 [SOURCE...] [N] [plan]   the same over the named sources (Alpine's four, Guix's
                                    two, and every built source of bs2lib/sources.py: the one-disk
                                    Linux corpus guests without ZFS or md; a skipped one is refused,
                                    naming the piece that builds it); --sweep N: N tier 0 cases a
                                    source (default 5 x N), --tier2 N: N tier 2 cases a UEFI source
                                    (default 5, Alpine's 30 in all)
  bs2 BackShot2 corpus [plan]       the corpus alone, at tier 0 (tier 1 with --tier 1)
  bs2 BackShot2All [plan]           every built source (bs2lib/sources.py built()) a host of the run
                                    holds, fresh (no ledger row excuses a case: the draws never read
                                    it), as bs2all-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS: 1,000 tier 0, 20 tier 1 and 5 tier 2
                                    (UEFI) a source, Alpine's four as BackShot2Alpine (200 tier 1
                                    each, its 30 tier 2); every unbuilt source and tier 3 SKIPPED,
                                    naming the piece that builds it (bs2lib/allrun.py), and a built
                                    source no host holds SKIPPED "not on any host in this run"; a
                                    manifest (RUN/bs2all.json) on each host; then prints the rest:
                                    (--sweep and --tier2 refused: decision 5's sizes are the word's)
  bs2 BackShot2All corpus RUN       ... the corpus at tier 1 as RUN-corpus, once RUN's queues finish
  bs2 BackShot2All leftovers RUN    ... then the leftovers set as RUN-lo on one host, detached
  bs2 BackShot2All report RUN [--json]   RUN's verdict: PASS, FAIL, HARNESS, INVALID per source and
                                    tier, the FAILs and their checks, the SKIPPED list, and FAIL,
                                    INCOMPLETE (a planned case, the corpus or the leftovers set with
                                    no verdict yet), PARTIAL PASS (anything SKIPPED) or PASS; --json:
                                    the same as JSON.  Its cases' ledger rows say word BackShot2All
  bs2 replay CASE [--tier N]        one case again, exactly
  bs2 shrink CASE [--tier N]        a failing case down to its smallest; saved in the corpus
  bs2 soak CASE N                   CASE N times at tier 1 (reported as K of N)
  bs2 leftovers [SET] [plan]        the leftovers set (bs2lib/leftovers.py): its restores in order
                                    onto one disk, on one host (chopin; --hosts H names another
                                    that has all three UEFI sources), detached; log in
                                    /bkoscratch/backshot2/logs/RUN.log, rows in RUN/leftovers.jsonl
  bs2 bin FROM                      copy FROM's /bkoscratch/backshot2/bin (the bko-holt, planner
                                    and caps.json under test) to the other hosts (--hosts: those)
  bs2 sync                          copy testvm/ and holt/ to the hosts' bs2-wt
  bs2 status RUN                    the run's verdicts so far, on each of its hosts and in all

  --hosts H,H|all (any word)        the hosts to use, of testvm/hosts.json's enabled ones
                                    (all: every one, the default).  Only a host whose
                                    vms/SOURCE is there takes SOURCE's cases (one read-only
                                    ls each: cage's cache has only alpine324), and only
                                    when its cmp-run.sh --ceiling holds the source's room
                                    (bs2lib/room.py need(): choubox's can't hold Guix's).  A
                                    source whose room is over every RAM-disk ceiling of the
                                    run (vanilla3, D 30) works on /bkoscratch (--reserve-ssd,
                                    HT_RAM=0), one case at a time, on the hosts whose
                                    holt_disk_mode is true (chopin, cinqcent) and whose memory
                                    ceiling holds it (room.py scratch()); plan says which

How a BackShot2 run spreads (split()): each source has a lead, its HOME host when that's
in the run, else the first that holds it.  The lead runs the source's tier 0 sweep and
draws its tier 1 and 2 cases (bs2-host enqueue --to), exactly as one host alone would;
bs2 spreads the cases over every host that holds the source, each to the one that would
finish it soonest for its slots (hosts.json's bs2_slots: big 5, small 2), so the hosts
finish about together, and copies each case file from the lead to its host.  Each host
gets its own queue.txt and runs it.  First every host is checked (bin/ alike everywhere,
the rescuers, ht1.sh's debs).  Then each host, on its own (start_hosts()): prepares the
sources it holds (bs2-host source, as root under cmp-run.sh --reserve 2 3, port 2949;
nothing to do when ready); if it leads, draws its sources' cases, as root outside the
reservations (light(): tier 0 is planning, no VM); and starts its queue (a lead after its
sweeps, also outside them) as soon as the cases it will run are drawn and copied, not
once every lead has drawn.  Its share is the split of the planned cases, as plan prints
it, each filled with the drawn case of its place in its list (fill()): the split the run
made after every draw before.  A host whose generation of a source differs from the
lead's, or that something else fails for, isn't started; the others run, and bs2 exits 1
naming it.

What a case reuses (ht1-bs2.sh; README "What a case reuses"): the source's preparation
(its boot, dump and backup, made by bs2-host source; the backup's repository bound
read-only into the case's share, not copied), a rescuer resumed from a saved state, and
quits in place of poweroffs.  BS2_REUSE_SOURCE, BS2_REUSE_BACKUP, BS2_REPO_BIND (0: the
repository copied, as before), BS2_RESCUER_STATE and BS2_FAST_DOWN set to 0 here turn
each off on the hosts.

Results: each host's /bkoscratch/backshot2/runs/RUN/ and Test2's ledger
(family bs2, word the run's: BS2_WORD).  "plan" prints the cases, tiers, each host's share and time, and runs nothing.
bs2-host takes ports 2943-2949 on whichever host runs it (the queue's slots the
first of 2943-2948, a source's preparing and a tier 1 by hand 2949): keep them free on
every host.
"""

import importlib.util
import json
import os
import re
import shlex
import subprocess
import sys
import time

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
if HERE not in sys.path:   # bs2lib, for a bs2 loaded as a module (Test2's tests), last: it shadows nothing
    sys.path.append(HERE)
REPO = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(HERE))
from bs2lib import allrun as AR, case as C, room as RM, sources as SRC, space as SP  # noqa: E402
# BackShot2's sources (bs2lib/sources.py, A2): BackShot2Alpine's four, Guix System's
# (bs2lib/families/guix.py), then every other built one of the corpus (one disk, Linux, no
# ZFS or md: OTHER_SOURCES, sorted; sources.classify() says why the rest are skipped and
# which piece takes each).  Each one's lead draws its cases, runs its tier 0, and is where
# replay, shrink and the corpus run; HOME deals each group in even turns over the lead
# hosts (Alpine's as before Guix's: two each; then the others'), group by group.
ALPINE_SOURCES = SRC.ALPINE_SOURCES
GUIX_SOURCES = SRC.GUIX_SOURCES
OTHER_SOURCES = SRC.others()
SOURCES = ALPINE_SOURCES + GUIX_SOURCES + OTHER_SOURCES
# The UEFI sources (their corpus dumps' firmware), whose cases that touch an ESP or the
# NVRAM go to tier 2 too.
UEFI = {s for s in SOURCES if SRC.uefi(s)}
# The tree on the hosts that bs2 copies testvm/ and holt/ to and runs bs2-host from:
# ~/backotter-work/BS2_WT (default bs2-wt), so two sessions' runs never share one.
WT = os.environ.get("BS2_WT") or "bs2-wt"
if not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*-wt", WT):
    sys.exit(f"bs2: BS2_WT={WT!r}: a name ending in -wt, of letters, digits, '.', '_' and '-'")


def _host_table():
    """testvm/test2/t2lib/hosts.py, the loader of the host table testvm/hosts.json, by its path."""
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("bs2_hosts_table", os.path.join(REPO, "testvm", "test2", "t2lib",
                                                                                   "hosts.py"))
    m = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    spec.loader.exec_module(m)
    return m


HOSTS_TABLE = _host_table()
# The hosts of this command: every enabled amd64 one (BackShot2's sources, its rescuer and
# bko-holt are amd64: an arm64 host such as bigfoot is never one), or --hosts' (use_hosts()).
RUN_HOSTS = {h: HOSTS_TABLE.ssh(h) for h in HOSTS_TABLE.names(arch="amd64")}
# The lead hosts, from the host table: its default amd64 hosts of the first class (the big
# ones).  Only they hold every source: BackShot2's sources are not published to the store,
# so a small host's cache has at most alpine324 (bs2 ls says which host has what), and a
# source is placed on a host that lacks it by no path here.  A table with none of them is a
# table to mend, not a run to deal to the small hosts: they would take sources whose cases
# they can't hold, and every case would then die on its host.
LEAD_HOSTS = [h for h in HOSTS_TABLE.names(default=True, arch="amd64") if HOSTS_TABLE.class_rank(h) == 0]
if not LEAD_HOSTS:
    sys.exit(f"bs2: testvm/hosts.json names no default amd64 host of class {list(HOSTS_TABLE.load()['classes'])[0]}: "
             "BackShot2's leads hold every source, and a small host's cache holds at most alpine324")


def deal(sources, hosts):
    """{source: host}: SOURCES in even turns over HOSTS, in order (4 sources over 2 hosts:
    the first two to the first host).  The share is how assign() shares them out too."""
    share = max(1, -(-len(sources) // max(1, len(hosts))))
    return {s: hosts[min(i // share, len(hosts) - 1)] for i, s in enumerate(sources)}


HOME = dict(deal(ALPINE_SOURCES, LEAD_HOSTS), **deal(GUIX_SOURCES, LEAD_HOSTS), **deal(OTHER_SOURCES, LEAD_HOSTS))
CHOSEN = False   # --hosts given: replay and the corpus go only where vms/SOURCE is
ALPINE = list(ALPINE_SOURCES)
ROOT = "/bkoscratch/backshot2"
HOST_WT = f"~/backotter-work/{WT}"
HOST_BS2 = f"{HOST_WT}/testvm/backshot2/bs2-host"
HOST_IOLOG = f"{HOST_WT}/testvm/compare/iolog.sh"   # (light()'s wear-log line)
ROOT_SBIN = "/usr/local/sbin:/usr/sbin:/sbin"   # (light()'s PATH: root's, before m's)
MAX_SLOTS = 6     # bs2-host queue's ports, 2943-2948 (2949: by hand)
SWEEP = 5         # tier 0's sweep: N * SWEEP new cases a source, on its lead
TIER2 = 30        # Alpine's tier 2 cases in all, shared by its UEFI sources (BackShot2Alpine's 30)
TIER2_EACH = 5    # every other UEFI source's (docs/design/bs2-all.md "What it runs")
COUNTS = {}       # --sweep N (tier 0 cases a source), --tier2 N (tier 2 cases a UEFI source): main()
# What held() learnt of each host: its cmp-run.sh --ceiling, and where each source's cases
# work there ({(host, source): "ram" or "ssd"}, bs2lib/room.py scratch()).
CEILINGS = {}
SCRATCH = {}
LISTED = {}   # {host: the sources its ls found, None: it didn't answer} (held(); missing_why())


def secs(source, tier):
    """Seconds a case of SOURCE takes at TIER (bs2lib/sources.py secs(): measured where bs2
    has run the source, else HoltTest1's seconds for its guest less what a case reuses)."""
    return SRC.secs(source, tier)[0]


def scratch_on(host, source):
    """Where SOURCE's cases work on HOST: "ram" (the RAM disk) or "ssd" (/bkoscratch), as
    held() found it; "ram" when held() didn't look (the tests' stand-ins)."""
    return SCRATCH.get((host, source), RM.RAM)


def use_hosts(arg):
    """--hosts H,H|all: RUN_HOSTS becomes those hosts (testvm/hosts.json's, in its order)."""
    global RUN_HOSTS, CHOSEN
    known = HOSTS_TABLE.names(arch="amd64")
    ns = list(known) if arg == "all" else [HOSTS_TABLE.short(x) for x in arg.replace(",", " ").split()]
    other = [n for n in ns if n in HOSTS_TABLE.known() and n not in known]
    if other:
        sys.exit(f"bs2: --hosts: {' '.join(other)}: not an amd64 host (testvm/hosts.json's arch), and BackShot2's "
                 f"sources are amd64 (of {HOSTS_TABLE.phrase(known)}, or all)")
    bad = [n for n in ns if n not in known]
    if bad or not ns:
        sys.exit(f"bs2: --hosts: no such host {' '.join(bad) or '(none named)'} (of {HOSTS_TABLE.phrase(known)}, or all)")
    RUN_HOSTS = {n: HOSTS_TABLE.ssh(n) for n in known if n in ns}
    CHOSEN = True


def slots(h):
    """H's queue slots: hosts.json's bs2_slots (big 5, small 2), at most MAX_SLOTS."""
    return min(MAX_SLOTS, HOSTS_TABLE.limit(h, "bs2_slots"))


def held(sources, hosts=None):
    """{host: set of SOURCES whose vms/SOURCE is there and whose cases the host's room can
    hold} over HOSTS (default RUN_HOSTS), an ls and a cmp-run.sh --ceiling each (roomy(),
    with the largest RAM-disk ceiling of those hosts: a source over every one of them works
    on /bkoscratch on a holt_disk_mode host, room.py scratch()); a host that doesn't
    answer holds none.  CEILINGS and SCRATCH keep what it found."""
    seen = {}
    for h in hosts or RUN_HOSTS:
        r = ssh(h, 'echo "@ceiling $(cd ~/backotter-work && ./cmp-run.sh --ceiling 2>/dev/null)"; '
                   "cd ~/backotter-work/vms 2>/dev/null && for g in " + " ".join(sources) +
                '; do [ -e "$g" ] && echo "$g"; done; true', check=False, capture=True)
        if r.returncode:
            print(f"bs2: {h} didn't answer: left out", file=sys.stderr)
            seen[h] = LISTED[h] = None
            continue
        seen[h] = ({w for line in r.stdout.splitlines() if not line.startswith("@") for w in line.split()},
                   ceiling_of(r.stdout))
        LISTED[h] = set(seen[h][0])
    run_disk = max((x[1][0] for x in seen.values() if x and x[1]), default=None)
    out = {}
    for h, x in seen.items():
        if x is None:
            out[h] = set()
            continue
        here, ceil = x
        CEILINGS[h] = ceil
        ok = disk_ok(h)
        out[h], dropped = roomy(here, ceil, run_disk, ok)
        for s in out[h]:
            SCRATCH[(h, s)] = RM.scratch(s, ceil, ok, run_disk)
        for s in sorted(dropped):
            d, m = RM.need(s)
            room = f"its cmp-run.sh --ceiling is {ceil[0]:g} {ceil[1]:g}" if ceil else "its cmp-run.sh --ceiling didn't answer"
            ssd = ""
            if ceil and d > ceil[0] and m <= ceil[1]:
                ssd = (" (a host of the run holds it in its RAM disk)" if run_disk is not None and d <= run_disk + RM.EPS else
                       " (and its holt_disk_mode isn't true in testvm/hosts.json: no SSD cases there)" if not ok else "")
            print(f"bs2: {h} has vms/{s}, but {room}, under {s}'s cases' --reserve {d} {m}: left out for {s}{ssd}",
                  file=sys.stderr)
    return out


def disk_ok(host):
    """Whether HOST takes cases on its SSD: its holt_disk_mode is true in testvm/hosts.json
    (Chopin and Cinqcent: bs2-all.md, one disk slot per big host; the small hosts' scratch_mode
    overflow alone doesn't)."""
    try:
        return HOSTS_TABLE.limit(host, "holt_disk_mode") is True
    except Exception:   # (a host the table doesn't know: no)
        return False


def ceiling_of(text):
    """(disk, memory) GiB of held()'s "@ceiling D M" line in TEXT; None when it has none or
    no figures (the host's cmp-run.sh --ceiling failed)."""
    for line in text.splitlines():
        if line.startswith("@ceiling"):
            w = line.split()[1:3]
            try:
                return float(w[0]), float(w[1])
            except (ValueError, IndexError):
                return None
    return None


def roomy(here, ceiling, run_disk=None, disk_ok=False):
    """(the sources of HERE a host whose cmp-run.sh --ceiling is CEILING can hold, the ones it
    can't): a source's cases reserve at least bs2lib/room.py need()'s (guix15's 7 GiB of RAM
    disk and 4 of memory), and cmp-run.sh refuses at once a --reserve over the ceiling ("can
    never fit here"), so such a case would leave no row on that host.  A host whose ceiling is
    unknown (None) holds none: its --reserve would be refused too (pick-host says the same).
    With DISK_OK (the host takes SSD cases: disk_ok()) a source whose disk is over RUN_DISK
    (the largest RAM-disk ceiling of the run's hosts) too is held when its memory fits: its
    cases work on /bkoscratch there (room.py scratch(): vanilla3's D 30)."""
    keep = {s for s in here if RM.scratch(s, ceiling, disk_ok, run_disk)}
    return keep, set(here) - keep


def missing_why(source, hosts=None):
    """Why no host of HOSTS (default RUN_HOSTS) holds SOURCE, in words, from what held()
    found (LISTED, CEILINGS): which hosts lack vms/SOURCE, which have it but whose
    cmp-run.sh --ceiling is under its cases' room (bs2lib/room.py need()), which didn't
    answer."""
    hosts = list(hosts or RUN_HOSTS)
    no = [h for h in hosts if h in LISTED and LISTED[h] is None]
    lack = [h for h in hosts if LISTED.get(h) is not None and source not in LISTED[h]]
    room = [h for h in hosts if LISTED.get(h) and source in LISTED[h]]
    out = []
    if lack:
        out.append(f"no vms/{source} on {', '.join(lack)}")
    if room:
        d, m = RM.need(source)
        out.append(f"on {', '.join(room)}, under its cases' --reserve {d:g} {m:g}: " + ", ".join(
            f"{h}'s cmp-run.sh --ceiling is {CEILINGS[h][0]:g} {CEILINGS[h][1]:g}" if CEILINGS.get(h) else
            f"{h}'s cmp-run.sh --ceiling didn't answer" for h in room))
    if no:
        out.append(f"{', '.join(no)} didn't answer")
    return "; ".join(out) or "no host of the run looked"


def holders(sources, have, hosts=None):
    """{source: [host...]}: the hosts (HOSTS' order, default RUN_HOSTS) that HAVE it; a
    source no host has: sys.exit."""
    hosts = list(hosts or RUN_HOSTS)
    can = {s: [h for h in hosts if s in have.get(h, ())] for s in sources}
    none = [s for s in sources if not can[s]]
    if none:
        sys.exit(f"bs2: no host of {', '.join(hosts)} has vms/{', vms/'.join(none)}")
    return can


def leads(can):
    """{source: host}: its HOME host when that holds it here, else the first that does."""
    return {s: HOME[s] if HOME.get(s) in hs else hs[0] for s, hs in can.items()}


def tier2_of(source, sources):
    """Tier 2 cases SOURCE draws in a run of SOURCES: none for a BIOS one (UEFI); --tier2's;
    else for Alpine's, TIER2 shared by the run's Alpine UEFI sources (BackShot2Alpine's 10
    each), and TIER2_EACH for every other."""
    if source not in UEFI:
        return 0
    if COUNTS.get("tier2") is not None:
        return COUNTS["tier2"]
    if source in ALPINE_SOURCES:
        return max(1, TIER2 // max(1, len([s for s in sources if s in UEFI and s in ALPINE_SOURCES])))
    return TIER2_EACH


def n_of(n, source):
    """Tier 1 cases SOURCE draws: N, or N[SOURCE] when N is {source: count} (BackShot2All's,
    bs2lib/allrun.py counts(): 200 an Alpine source, 20 the rest)."""
    return n.get(source, 0) if isinstance(n, dict) else n


def sweep_n(n, source=None):
    """Tier 0 cases a source's sweep draws: --sweep's, else its tier 1 count (n_of()) * SWEEP."""
    return COUNTS["sweep"] if COUNTS.get("sweep") is not None else n_of(n, source) * SWEEP


def jobs_of(sources, n):
    """The run's cases as (source, tier, i), in the order the leads draw them."""
    out = []
    for s in sources:
        out += [(s, 1, i) for i in range(n_of(n, s))]
        out += [(s, 2, i) for i in range(tier2_of(s, sources))]
    return out


def sweep_secs(sources, n, lead):
    """{host: seconds}: the tier 0 sweeps each lead runs before its queue."""
    out = {}
    for s in sources:
        out[lead[s]] = out.get(lead[s], 0) + sweep_n(n, s) * secs(s, 0)
    return out


def split(jobs, can, nslots, start=None):
    """{host: [job...]}: JOBS ((source, tier, x), in the run's order) spread over the hosts
    that hold each one's source (CAN: {source: [host...]}).  Each goes to the host that would
    finish it soonest (finish()): its START seconds, its slots busy, plus what it has so far,
    plus the job, over its NSLOTS, and its SSD lane's cases (scratch_on(): one at a time,
    bs2-host's ssd_token) one after another; NSLOTS' order on a tie; the sources on the fewest
    hosts first, and the longer case first (secs(): each source's own seconds at each tier),
    so the hosts finish about together and in proportion to their slots where they hold the
    same sources.  Every job goes to exactly one host; each host's keep JOBS' order.  A job
    whose source no host of NSLOTS holds: ValueError."""
    hosts = list(nslots)
    st = {h: float((start or {}).get(h, 0)) for h in hosts}
    busy = {h: st[h] * nslots[h] for h in hosts}   # slot-seconds
    lane = dict(st)                                # the SSD lane's end
    got = {h: [] for h in hosts}
    order = sorted(range(len(jobs)), key=lambda i: (len(can[jobs[i][0]]), -secs(jobs[i][0], jobs[i][1]), i))
    for i in order:
        s, t = jobs[i][0], jobs[i][1]
        hs = [h for h in can.get(s, ()) if h in busy]
        if not hs:
            raise ValueError(f"no host of {', '.join(hosts)} holds {s}")
        x = secs(s, t)

        def finish(y):
            ssd = scratch_on(y, s) == RM.SSD
            return max((busy[y] + x) / nslots[y], lane[y] + x if ssd else lane[y])
        h = min(hs, key=lambda y: (finish(y), hosts.index(y)))
        busy[h] += x
        if scratch_on(h, s) == RM.SSD:
            lane[h] += x
        got[h].append(i)
    return {h: [jobs[i] for i in sorted(got[h])] for h in hosts}


def wall(jobs, nslots, start=0, host=None):
    """Seconds a host takes for JOBS on NSLOTS slots, after START (its sweeps): their seconds
    over the slots, never less than its longest case (a case is one slot's), nor than its SSD
    cases one after another (HOST's, scratch_on(): bs2-host runs one at a time)."""
    xs = [secs(s, t) for s, t, _ in jobs]
    lane = sum(secs(s, t) for s, t, _ in jobs if host and scratch_on(host, s) == RM.SSD)
    return start + max(sum(xs) / nslots, max(xs, default=0), lane)


def ssh(host, cmd, check=True, capture=False, input=None):
    r = subprocess.run(["ssh", "-o", "ConnectTimeout=10", RUN_HOSTS.get(host) or HOSTS_TABLE.ssh(host), cmd], text=True,
                       capture_output=capture, input=input)
    if check and r.returncode:
        sys.exit(f"bs2: {host}: {cmd[:80]}... exit {r.returncode}{(': ' + r.stderr[-400:]) if capture else ''}")
    return r


def par(cmds):
    """{host: cmd} run at once, one ssh each; {host: (exit, stdout, stderr)}."""
    import threading
    out = {}

    def one(h, c):
        r = subprocess.run(["ssh", "-o", "ConnectTimeout=10", RUN_HOSTS.get(h) or HOSTS_TABLE.ssh(h), c], text=True,
                           capture_output=True, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
        out[h] = (r.returncode, r.stdout, r.stderr)

    ts = [threading.Thread(target=one, args=(h, c)) for h, c in cmds.items()]
    for t in ts:
        t.start()
    for t in ts:
        t.join()
    return {h: out[h] for h in cmds}


def sync(hosts=None):
    for h in hosts or RUN_HOSTS:
        subprocess.run(["rsync", "-a", "--delete", "--exclude", "target", "--exclude", "__pycache__",
                        f"{REPO}/holt", f"{REPO}/testvm", f"{RUN_HOSTS.get(h) or HOSTS_TABLE.ssh(h)}:backotter-work/{WT}/"],
                       check=True)


# What a case reuses (ht1-bs2.sh), each on unless set to 0: set here, passed on to the
# hosts' cases (the queue, replay, soak, the corpus) so a run can compare.
REUSE_VARS = ("BS2_REUSE_SOURCE", "BS2_REUSE_BACKUP", "BS2_REPO_BIND", "BS2_RESCUER_STATE", "BS2_FAST_DOWN")
# Passed on the same way: BS2_HOLT, the bko-holt a case runs (a path on the hosts; bs2-host's
# default is /bkoscratch/backshot2/bin/bko-holt), so a fix can be run before it is in bin/;
# and BS2_WORD, the word of the run (main() sets it), which each case's ledger rows name
# (bs2lib/ledger.py word_of(): through light()'s draws and sweeps, the queue's cmp-run.sh and
# sudo -E, to bs2-host tier1 and tier0's write_rows).
PASS_VARS = REUSE_VARS + ("BS2_HOLT", "BS2_WORD")


def reuse_env():
    """PASS_VARS set in this environment, as "NAME=VALUE " words for a host's command."""
    return "".join(f"{v}={shlex.quote(os.environ[v])} " for v in PASS_VARS if v in os.environ)


def reserve_tier1(case):
    """The start of CASE's tier 1 by hand (replay, soak, the corpus), in ~/backotter-work: as
    root under the cmp-run.sh reservation bs2-host reserve --words gives it (--reserve of the
    RAM disk and memory: its inode tables on LUKS, bs2lib/case.py disk_gib; its source's
    room, bs2lib/room.py, at least 3 GiB of memory; or --reserve-ssd for a source whose room
    is over the host's RAM disk, which bs2-host tier1 then runs on /bkoscratch, room.py
    scratch(), one at a time: bs2-host lane takes the host's SSD lane before cmp-run.sh's
    reservation, and holds it while the case runs); the --tier and the rest follow."""
    return (f"R=$({HOST_BS2} reserve {case} --mem 3 --words) && {reuse_env()}{HOST_BS2} lane {case} -- ./cmp-run.sh $R "
            f"sudo -E {HOST_BS2} tier1 {case}")


def root(cmd, reserve="2 2", tag="bs2:mac"):
    """CMD as root under a reservation, as m submits it (cmp-run.sh as m)."""
    return f"cd ~/backotter-work && WEAR_TAG={tag} {reuse_env()}./cmp-run.sh --reserve {reserve} sudo -E {cmd}"


def placement(sources, n, have=None):
    """What a run of N cases a source does where: (can, lead, {host: jobs}, {host: sweep s});
    HAVE: held()'s, when the caller has it already."""
    have = held(sources) if have is None else have
    can = holders(sources, have)
    lead = leads(can)
    use = [h for h in RUN_HOSTS if any(h in hs for hs in can.values())]
    start = sweep_secs(sources, n, lead)
    parts = split(jobs_of(sources, n), can, {h: slots(h) for h in use}, start)
    return can, lead, parts, start


def scratch_words(s, hosts):
    """SOURCE's place on HOSTS in a plan's words: RAM, SSD, or RAM but SSD on some."""
    ssd = [h for h in hosts if scratch_on(h, s) == RM.SSD]
    if not ssd:
        return "RAM"
    if len(ssd) == len(hosts):
        return "SSD"
    return f"RAM, SSD on {', '.join(ssd)}"


def plan_words(sources, n, have=None):
    """The plan of a run of SOURCES, N cases a source (n_of()), as plan prints it; returns
    its slowest host's seconds."""
    can, lead, parts, start = placement(sources, n, have)
    w = max([16] + [len(s) + 1 for s in sources])

    def sec(s, t):
        x, kind = SRC.secs(s, t)
        return f"{x:g} {kind}"

    print(f"{'source':{w}} {'lead':9} {'tier0':>6} {'tier1':>6} {'tier2':>6}  {'tier 1 s':13} {'tier 2 s':13} {'scratch':8} hosts")
    for s in sources:
        t2 = tier2_of(s, sources)
        print(f"{s:{w}} {lead[s]:9} {sweep_n(n, s):6} {n_of(n, s):6} {t2:6}  {sec(s, 1):13} {sec(s, 2) if t2 else '-':13} "
              f"{scratch_words(s, can[s]):8} {', '.join(can[s])}")
    longest = 0
    for h, js in parts.items():
        if not js:
            print(f"{h}: none of these sources' cases")
            continue
        by = []
        for s in sources:
            c1 = sum(1 for x in js if x[0] == s and x[1] == 1)
            c2 = sum(1 for x in js if x[0] == s and x[1] == 2)
            if c1 or c2:
                by.append(f"{s} {c1}" + (f"+{c2}" if c2 else "") + (" SSD" if scratch_on(h, s) == RM.SSD else ""))
        sec_ = wall(js, slots(h), start.get(h, 0), h)
        longest = max(longest, sec_)
        sw = f", after its tier 0 sweeps (~{start[h] / 60:.0f} min)" if start.get(h) else ""
        print(f"{h}: {slots(h)} slots, {len(js)} cases ({'; '.join(by)}), ~{sec_ / 3600:.1f} h est.{sw}")
    print(f"the run: ~{longest / 3600:.1f} h est. (its slowest host, by each source's seconds a case above), each host "
          f"after ~5-15 min of preparing what it lacks and the leads drawing its cases")
    print(wear_words(sources, parts))
    return longest


def wear_words(sources, parts):
    """The plan's wear line: how many cases work on the SSD, and about what they write there
    (HoltTest1's gb_disk for the guest a case, testvm/test2/estimates.tsv, else its D; at most
    its D a case, room.py need(): what the case reserves of the SSD)."""
    on, n, est, top = {}, 0, 0.0, 0.0
    for h, js in parts.items():
        for s, _, _ in js:
            if scratch_on(h, s) != RM.SSD:
                continue
            if h not in on.setdefault(s, []):
                on[s].append(h)
            n += 1
            d = RM.need(s)[0] * 1.074   # (GiB to GB)
            g = SRC.disk_gb(s)
            est += min(g, d) if g is not None else d
            top += d
    if not n:
        return "in RAM: ~0 GB written to the SSDs (records only, ~5 MB a case)"
    what = "; ".join(f"{s} on {', '.join(on[s])}" for s in sources if s in on)
    return (f"on the SSD (/bkoscratch, cmp-run.sh --reserve-ssd): {n} cases ({what}), ~{est:.0f} GB written est. "
            f"(HoltTest1's gb_disk a case, testvm/test2/estimates.tsv), at most ~{top:.0f} GB (its D a case); "
            f"the rest in RAM: ~0 GB written to the SSDs (records only, ~5 MB a case)")


# ---- /bkoscratch: what a run puts there, host by host (bs2lib/space.py) -------------------

def rooms_of(sources_of):
    """{host: bs2-host room's facts (free bytes, each source's preparation and tools there),
    or None when it didn't answer} for SOURCES_OF ({host: [source...]}), at once, as root
    (it reads root's files: sudo -n, no reservation), with BS2_HOLT passed on (whether a
    preparation is current depends on the bko-holt under test)."""
    cmds = {h: f"cd ~/backotter-work && sudo -n -E env PATH=\"{ROOT_SBIN}:$PATH\" {reuse_env()}{HOST_BS2} room "
               f"{' '.join(ss)}" for h, ss in sources_of.items()}
    out = {}
    for h, (rc, so, se) in par(cmds).items():
        try:
            out[h] = json.loads(so.strip().splitlines()[-1]) if rc == 0 else None
        except (ValueError, IndexError):
            out[h] = None
    return out


def ssd_peak(h, js):
    """The bytes H's SSD lane holds at once: its largest SSD case's (room.py need()'s D:
    one at a time, bs2-host ssd_token()), 0 with none there."""
    return max((RM.need(s)[0] * SP.GiB for s in {x[0] for x in js} if scratch_on(h, s) == RM.SSD), default=0)


def space_of(sources, can, lead, parts, rooms, margin=None):
    """{host: (Need, its free bytes or None, why it doesn't fit or None)} for the hosts of
    PARTS: each prepares every source of SOURCES it holds (CAN), copies the tools of the
    ones it leads whose tier 0 has dry runs (tools_of()) and drops the rest, then runs its
    cases (its SSD lane, records): bs2lib/space.py need(), from ROOMS (rooms_of())."""
    margin = SP.MARGIN_GIB if margin is None else margin
    out = {}
    for h in parts:
        mine = [s for s in sources if h in can.get(s, ())]
        led = [s for s in mine if lead.get(s) == h]
        r = rooms.get(h)
        n = SP.need(mine, tools_of(led), (r or {}).get("sources") or {}, ssd_peak(h, parts[h]), len(parts[h]))
        free = r.get("free") if r else None
        out[h] = (n, free, SP.check(n, free, margin))
    return out


def margin_gib():
    """BS2_SPACE_MARGIN_GIB, else space.py's MARGIN_GIB (30)."""
    try:
        return float(os.environ.get("BS2_SPACE_MARGIN_GIB", SP.MARGIN_GIB))
    except ValueError:
        sys.exit("bs2: BS2_SPACE_MARGIN_GIB: a number of GiB")


def space_words(space, sources):
    """The plan's lines for SPACE (space_of()), a host each."""
    lines = [f"/bkoscratch (bs2lib/space.py: preparations and tools per space-sizes.tsv, measured, else the "
             f"corpus dump's used bytes x the 90th percentile of the measured ratios; tools on a source's lead only; margin "
             f"{margin_gib():g} GiB):"]
    for h, (n, free, why) in space.items():
        f = f"{free / SP.GiB:.0f} GiB free" if free is not None else "free unknown (bs2-host room didn't answer)"
        if free is None:
            why_w = "not checked (its tree may predate bs2-host room: a run syncs it, then checks, and refuses this)"
        else:
            why_w = "OK" if not why else "REFUSED: " + why
        top = "; ".join(n.lines[:4]) + (f"; +{len(n.lines) - 4} more" if len(n.lines) > 4 else "")
        est = f"; est. for {len(n.est)} not in space-sizes.tsv" if n.est else ""
        lines.append(f"  {h}: peak +{n.peak / SP.GiB:.0f} GiB (once prepared {n.end / SP.GiB:+.0f}, SSD lane "
                     f"{n.ssd / SP.GiB:.0f}, records {n.records / SP.GiB:.1f}), {f}: {why_w}"
                     f"{' (' + top + est + ')' if top else ''}")
    return lines


def space_check(sources, n, can, lead, parts, plan=False):
    """The space preflight: SPACE's lines printed; when not PLAN, sys.exit naming each host
    that lacks room (its need and free), before anything is written or started there."""
    rooms = rooms_of({h: [s for s in sources if h in can.get(s, ())] for h in parts})
    space = space_of(sources, can, lead, parts, rooms, margin_gib())
    for line in space_words(space, sources):
        print(line)
    bad = {h: why for h, (_, _, why) in space.items() if why}
    if bad and not plan:
        sys.exit("bs2: not started: /bkoscratch lacks room (bs2lib/space.py; BS2_SPACE_MARGIN_GIB sets the margin):\n  " +
                 "\n  ".join(f"{h}: {w}" for h, w in bad.items()))
    return space


def space_plan(sources, n, have):
    """The plan's space lines (space_check(), PLAN: never an exit) for a run of SOURCES,
    N cases a source, on the hosts HAVE (held()'s) says hold them, placed as the run would."""
    can, lead, parts, _ = placement(sources, n, have)
    use = [h for h, js in parts.items() if js or h in lead.values()]
    can = {s: [h for h in hs if h in use] for s, hs in can.items()}
    return space_check(sources, n, can, lead, {h: parts.get(h, []) for h in use}, plan=True)


def preflight(hosts):
    """Each host has what a case needs, and the same bin/ as the others: else sys.exit, naming what."""
    need = ["~/backotter-work/cmp-run.sh", "~/backotter-work/bko-bin/linux/rustic-bko",
            "~/backotter-work/vms/debian13/id_ed25519", "~/backotter-work/vms/ubuntu26-uefi/id_ed25519",
            "/bkoscratch/holttest1d/rescuer/rescuer.qcow2", "/bkoscratch/holttest1d/rescuer/rescuer-uefi.qcow2"]
    cmd = ("for f in " + " ".join(need) + '; do [ -e "$f" ] || echo "missing $f"; done; '
           "for p in f2fs-tools jfsutils; do ls /bkoscratch/holttest1d/bin/${p}_*.deb >/dev/null 2>&1 || "
           'echo "missing /bkoscratch/holttest1d/bin/${p}_*.deb (ht1.sh refuses without it)"; done; '
           f"for f in bko-holt bs2_plan caps.json; do echo \"bin $f $(sha256sum < {ROOT}/bin/$f 2>/dev/null | cut -c1-64)\"; done")
    bins, bad = {}, []
    for h, (rc, out, err) in par({h: cmd for h in hosts}).items():
        if rc:
            bad.append(f"{h}: no answer ({err.strip()[-200:]})")
            continue
        for line in out.splitlines():
            if line.startswith("missing "):
                bad.append(f"{h}: {line}")
            elif line.startswith("bin "):
                _, f, *sha = line.split()
                if not sha:
                    bad.append(f"{h}: missing {ROOT}/bin/{f}")
                bins.setdefault(h, {})[f] = sha[0] if sha else None
    kinds = {tuple(sorted(b.items())) for b in bins.values()}
    if len(kinds) > 1:
        bad.append("the hosts' " + ROOT + "/bin differ (" + "; ".join(
            f"{h}: bko-holt {(b.get('bko-holt') or 'none')[:12]}" for h, b in bins.items()) + "): bs2 bin FROM copies one host's")
    if bad:
        sys.exit("bs2: not started:\n  " + "\n  ".join(bad))


def light(host, cmd, tag):
    """CMD as root on HOST outside cmp-run.sh's reservations: tier 0's planning (a lead
    drawing its cases, its sweeps), which runs no VM.  What it uses (the wear log,
    /bkoscratch/wear/jobs.log, 2026-11-17 and 2026-11-18 on chopin and cinqcent): one
    CPU (the planner runs --test-threads 1, the dry runs one at a time), a memory peak of
    50-150 MB, 0.1-12 MB written to the SSD (the case files and the rows), and in RAM only
    the dry runs' sparse scratch files, a few at once, each dropped after it is read;
    60-70 s a 200-case list, ~5 min a 1000-case sweep.  Under a --reserve 2 2 it waited
    for room it never used: on 2026-11-18 chopin's draws waited ~1h45m behind other
    jobs, and every host's queue with them.  Still in a scope of its own, in the host's
    job slice, under iolog.sh: its wear-log line, tagged TAG, as under cmp-run.sh.
    Its PATH is root's sbin dirs (ROOT_SBIN) before m's: "$PATH" expands in m's ssh
    shell, which has no sbin on Debian, and the dry runs' sfdisk, mkfs and the like are
    there (root()'s commands get them from sudo's secure_path)."""
    sl = HOSTS_TABLE.job_slice(host)
    return (f"cd ~/backotter-work && sudo -E systemd-run --quiet --scope --collect{' --slice=' + sl if sl else ''}"
            f" -p IOAccounting=yes env PATH=\"{ROOT_SBIN}:$PATH\" WEAR_TAG={tag} {reuse_env()}{HOST_IOLOG}"
            f" {shlex.quote('light ' + cmd)} -- {cmd}")


def prep_cmd(h, ss, run, tools=()):
    """The one command that has H make the run's directories and prepare SS, the sources
    it holds (bs2-host source: once per generation, and again when the bko-holt or the
    harness that made the preparation changed: what its cases reuse), printing a "gen
    SOURCE GEN" line each.  A preparation may boot the source: under a reservation.  TOOLS:
    the sources whose tier 0 H runs (it leads them: tools_of()), whose tools it copies
    (--tools); every other's it removes (--drop-tools: no tier 0 of it runs there)."""
    # (The RAM disk's dir as m: made first by a root job after a reboot, it was
    # root's, and tier 0, which runs as m, couldn't write there.)
    c = [f"mkdir -p {ROOT}/logs {ROOT}/runs /mnt/bko-ram/backshot2"]
    c += [root(f"{HOST_BS2} source {s} --port 2949 {'--tools' if s in tools else '--drop-tools'}", prep_room(s),
               f"bs2:{run}:source-{s}") for s in ss]
    c += [f'echo "gen {s} $(cat {ROOT}/sources/{s}/gen)"' for s in ss]
    return " && ".join(c)


def prep_room(source):
    """A preparation's --reserve: 2 GiB of the RAM disk (it works on /bkoscratch), and the
    source's memory (bs2lib/room.py: 3 GiB, or HoltTest1's for its guest if more).  A
    source whose cases work on /bkoscratch (room.py scratch(): vanilla3) prepares the same
    way: every preparation is HT_RAM=0, its 2 GiB only copy_tools' scratch mounts."""
    return f"2 {max(3, RM.of(source)[1])}"


def wants_tools(source):
    """Whether SOURCE's tier 0 has dry runs, so its lead needs its tools: its family's tier0
    is "chroot" (bs2-host tools_wanted(), from its corpus dump here; NixOS's is "plan").
    Alpine's three variants have no dump: alpine324's family.  No dump at all: yes."""
    from bs2lib import families
    d = SRC.dump(source) or (SRC.dump("alpine324") if source in ALPINE_SOURCES else None)
    return d is None or families.hooks(None, d).tier0 == "chroot"


def tools_of(led):
    """The sources of LED (a host's: the ones it leads, whose draws and tier 0 sweep it
    runs) whose tools it copies: those whose tier 0 has dry runs (wants_tools())."""
    return {s for s in led if wants_tools(s)}


def prepare_one(h, ss, run, tools=()):
    """H prepares SS (prep_cmd, TOOLS' tools copied): ({source: generation}, None), or (what
    it printed, the error)."""
    rc, out, err = par({h: prep_cmd(h, ss, run, tools)})[h]
    gens = {}
    for line in out.splitlines():
        if line.startswith("gen "):
            _, s, *g = line.split()
            gens[s] = g[0] if g else None
    return gens, (f"preparing its sources: exit {rc}: {(out + err).strip()[-300:]}" if rc else None)


def draw_cmd(lead_host, ss, sources, n, run):
    """The one command that has a lead draw its sources SS' cases, as one host alone would
    (enqueue --to: tier 1, then tier 2 for a UEFI source), outside the reservations
    (light()), one list after another, and print them (grep -H)."""
    rd = f"{ROOT}/runs/{run}"
    c = []
    for s in ss:
        c.append(light(lead_host, f"{HOST_BS2} enqueue {s} {n_of(n, s)} --tier 1 --run {run} --to {rd}/pick-{s}-t1.txt",
                       f"bs2:{run}:pick"))
        if tier2_of(s, sources):
            c.append(light(lead_host, f"{HOST_BS2} enqueue {s} {tier2_of(s, sources)} --tier 2 --run {run} --from 500000"
                                      f" --to {rd}/pick-{s}-t2.txt", f"bs2:{run}:pick"))
    c += [f"sudo mkdir -p {rd}-t0", f"sudo chown -R m: {rd} {rd}-t0",
          f"cd {rd} && {{ {' '.join(f'grep -H . pick-{s}-t[12].txt;' for s in ss)} true; }}"]
    return " && ".join(c)


def draw(lead_host, ss, sources, n, run):
    """The lead draws SS' cases (draw_cmd): ({(source, tier): [path...]}, None), or ({}, the error)."""
    rc, out, err = par({lead_host: draw_cmd(lead_host, ss, sources, n, run)})[lead_host]
    if rc:
        return {}, f"drawing the cases: exit {rc}: {(out + err).strip()[-400:]}"
    picks = {}
    for s, t, p in picks_of(out, ss):
        picks.setdefault((s, t), []).append(p)
    return picks, None


def fill(js, picks):
    """JS, a host's share of the run's planned cases (source, tier, i), as (source, tier, path):
    the i-th case of the source's tier T list, in JS' order; and how many had no such case
    (the lead drew fewer than asked)."""
    out, short = [], 0
    for s, t, i in js:
        got = picks.get((s, t), [])
        if i < len(got):
            out.append((s, t, got[i]))
        else:
            short += 1
    return out, short


def ship(h, js, lead, run):
    """JS' case files from their leads to H, and H's queue.txt (JS' order)."""
    rd = f"{ROOT}/runs/{run}"
    for L in sorted({lead[s] for s, _, _ in js} - {h}):
        names = sorted({os.path.basename(p) for s, _, p in js if lead[s] == L})
        src = subprocess.Popen(["ssh", RUN_HOSTS[L], f"cd {rd}/cases && tar -cf - {' '.join(names)}"], stdout=subprocess.PIPE)
        dst = subprocess.run(["ssh", RUN_HOSTS[h], f"mkdir -p {rd}/cases && tar -C {rd}/cases -xf -"], stdin=src.stdout)
        src.stdout.close()
        if src.wait() or dst.returncode:
            raise RuntimeError(f"copying {len(names)} cases from {L} failed")
    if js:
        r = ssh(h, f"mkdir -p {rd} && cat > {rd}/queue.txt", check=False, input="".join(f"{t} {p}\n" for _, t, p in js))
        if r.returncode:
            raise RuntimeError(f"writing its queue.txt: exit {r.returncode}")


def launch(h, js, sweeps, n, run):
    """H's chain, detached: the tier 0 sweeps (N * SWEEP cases each, outside the
    reservations) of SWEEPS, the sources it leads, then its queue of JS.  (A sweep that
    fails is in the log; the host's cases run regardless.)  False: nothing to start."""
    rd = f"{ROOT}/runs/{run}"
    c = [f"{{ {light(h, f'{HOST_BS2} tier0 {s} {sweep_n(n, s)} --run {run}-t0 --keep-passes 50', f'bs2:{run}:tier0')}; }}"
         for s in sweeps if sweep_n(n, s)]
    if sweeps:
        c.append(f"sudo chown -R m: {rd}-t0")
    if js:
        c.append(f"{reuse_env()}{HOST_BS2} queue {run} --slots {slots(h)}")
    if not c:
        return False
    r = ssh(h, f"setsid -f bash -c {json.dumps('; '.join(c))} > {ROOT}/logs/{run}.log 2>&1 < /dev/null", check=False)
    if r.returncode:
        raise RuntimeError(f"starting its queue: exit {r.returncode}")
    return True


def start_hosts(sources, n, run, can, lead, parts):
    """Each host of PARTS ({host: its planned cases (source, tier, i)}: split() of the
    run's jobs_of(), as plan prints it) starts its queue as soon as the cases it will run
    are drawn, not once every lead has drawn every source's: each host in a thread of
    its own.  A host prepares the sources it holds (CAN: {source: [host...]}); a lead
    (LEAD: {source: host}) then draws its sources' cases, outside the reservations; a
    host then waits for the leads of the sources it holds to have prepared them, checks
    it has each at its lead's generation (the cases are drawn on that), waits for the
    sources its cases are of to be drawn, takes its cases from the pick lists (fill()),
    has their files copied from their leads, and starts (a lead's tier 0 sweeps first).
    A host something fails for (its preparing, a lead's preparing or drawing, a
    generation that differs from its lead's, the copy) isn't started; the others are.
    Prints as each host draws and starts; returns {host: why} of those not started."""
    import threading
    hosts = list(parts)
    mine = {h: [s for s in sources if h in can.get(s, ())] for h in hosts}
    led = {}
    for s in sources:
        led.setdefault(lead[s], []).append(s)
    prepped = {h: threading.Event() for h in hosts}
    drawn = {s: threading.Event() for s in sources}
    gens, ready, picks, drew, why = {}, set(), {}, set(), {}
    lock = threading.Lock()

    def say(msg):
        with lock:
            print(msg, flush=True)

    def one(h):
        try:
            g, err = prepare_one(h, mine[h], run, tools_of(led.get(h, [])))
            gens[h] = g
            if err:
                why[h] = err
                return
            ready.add(h)
            prepped[h].set()
            if led.get(h):
                p, err = draw(h, led[h], sources, n, run)
                if not err:
                    with lock:
                        picks.update(p)
                        drew.update(led[h])
                for s in led[h]:   # (now: the hosts waiting for them needn't wait for this one)
                    drawn[s].set()
                if err:
                    why[h] = err
                    return
                say(f"{h}: drew the cases of {', '.join(led[h])}")
            for s in mine[h]:
                prepped[lead[s]].wait()
                if lead[s] not in ready:
                    why[h] = f"its lead {lead[s]} didn't prepare {s}"
                    return
                if gens.get(lead[s], {}).get(s) != gens[h].get(s):
                    why[h] = (f"its {s} is at {gens[h].get(s)}, its lead {lead[s]}'s at {gens.get(lead[s], {}).get(s)}: "
                              f"a source's cases are drawn on its lead's generation (refresh vms/{s}, or leave {h} out "
                              f"with --hosts)")
                    return
            need = sorted({s for s, _, _ in parts[h]}, key=sources.index)
            for s in need:
                drawn[s].wait()
            undrawn = [s for s in need if s not in drew]
            if undrawn:
                why[h] = (f"no cases of {', '.join(undrawn)}: not drawn (see its lead "
                          f"{', '.join(sorted({lead[s] for s in undrawn}))})")
                return
            js, short = fill(parts[h], picks)
            ship(h, js, lead, run)
            if launch(h, js, led.get(h, []), n, run):
                what = ", ".join(f"{s} {sum(1 for x in js if x[0] == s)}" for s in sources if any(x[0] == s for x in js))
                sw = f", after the tier 0 sweep of {', '.join(led[h])}" if led.get(h) else ""
                say(f"{h}: started {len(js)} cases on {slots(h)} slots ({what or 'none'}){sw}"
                    f"{f'; {short} planned cases had none drawn (a lead drew fewer than asked)' if short else ''}"
                    f" (log {ROOT}/logs/{run}.log)")
        except Exception as e:   # (a thread's error is its host's, never the others')
            why.setdefault(h, f"{type(e).__name__}: {e}")
        finally:   # (so no host waits for ever on one that failed)
            prepped[h].set()
            for s in led.get(h, []):
                drawn[s].set()

    ts = [threading.Thread(target=one, args=(h,), daemon=True) for h in hosts]   # (daemons: a ^C ends bs2)
    for t in ts:
        t.start()
    for t in ts:
        t.join()
    return why


def picks_of(text, sources):
    """The leads' pick lists (grep -H's "pick-SOURCE-tT.txt:T PATH" lines) as (source, tier,
    path), in SOURCES' order, tier 1 before 2, each list in its own order."""
    jobs = []
    for line in text.splitlines():
        m = re.match(r"pick-(.+)-t([12])\.txt:([12]) (\S+)$", line)
        if m and m.group(1) in sources:
            jobs.append((m.group(1), int(m.group(3)), m.group(4)))
    order = {s: i for i, s in enumerate(sources)}
    return sorted(jobs, key=lambda j: (order[j[0]], j[1]))


def run_words(sources, n, run, have=None, manifest=None):
    """Starts a run of SOURCES (N cases a source, n_of()) as RUN; HAVE: held()'s, when the
    caller has it already; MANIFEST (BackShot2All's): written to each of the run's hosts as
    ROOT/runs/RUN/bs2all.json, with its hosts, before any starts."""
    can, lead, parts, _ = placement(sources, n, have)
    use = [h for h, js in parts.items() if js or h in lead.values()]
    preflight(use)
    sync(use)
    can = {s: [h for h in hs if h in use] for s, hs in can.items()}
    space_check(sources, n, can, lead, {h: parts.get(h, []) for h in use})
    if manifest is not None:
        write_manifest(dict(manifest, hosts=use), use, run)
    print(f"preparing, drawing and starting each host as its cases are drawn: "
          f"{'; '.join(f'{h} {len(parts.get(h, []))} cases' for h in use)}")
    why = start_hosts(sources, n, run, can, lead, {h: parts.get(h, []) for h in use})
    if why:
        sys.exit(f"bs2: run {run}: not started on {len(why)} of {len(use)} hosts"
                 f"{f' (the others run: bs2 status {run})' if len(why) < len(use) else ''}:\n  " +
                 "\n  ".join(f"{h} ({len(parts.get(h, []))} cases): {w}" for h, w in sorted(why.items(), key=lambda x: use.index(x[0]))))
    print(f"run {run}: bs2 status {run}")


def status(run):
    """Each host's verdicts and queue for RUN, then the run's in all."""
    tot, started, queued = {}, 0, 0
    for h in RUN_HOSTS:
        r = ssh(h, f"cat {ROOT}/runs/{run}*/tier*.jsonl 2>/dev/null; echo \"@queue $(cat {ROOT}/runs/{run}/queue.next "
                   f"2>/dev/null) $(grep -c . {ROOT}/runs/{run}/queue.txt 2>/dev/null)\"",
                check=False, capture=True)
        counts = {}
        q = None
        for line in r.stdout.splitlines():
            if line.startswith("@queue "):
                q = [int(x) if x.isdigit() else 0 for x in (line[len("@queue "):].split(" ") + ["", ""])[:2]]
                continue
            try:
                j = json.loads(line)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            k = (j["source"], j["tier"], j["verdict"])
            counts[k] = counts.get(k, 0) + 1
            tot[k] = tot.get(k, 0) + 1
        for k in sorted(counts):
            print(f"{h:9} {k[0]:18} tier {k[1]} {k[2]:8} {counts[k]}")
        if q and q[1]:
            print(f"{h:9} queue: {min(q[0], q[1])} of {q[1]} started")
            started, queued = started + min(q[0], q[1]), queued + q[1]
    for k in sorted(tot):
        print(f"{'all':9} {k[0]:18} tier {k[1]} {k[2]:8} {tot[k]}")
    if queued:
        print(f"{'all':9} queue: {started} of {queued} started")


def bin_words(frm):
    """FROM's ROOT/bin (bko-holt, bs2_plan, caps.json) to the other hosts."""
    frm = HOSTS_TABLE.short(frm)
    if frm not in HOSTS_TABLE.known():
        sys.exit(f"bs2: bin: no such host {frm}")
    for h in RUN_HOSTS:
        if h == frm:
            continue
        src = subprocess.Popen(["ssh", HOSTS_TABLE.ssh(frm), f"tar -C {ROOT}/bin -cf - bko-holt bs2_plan caps.json"],
                               stdout=subprocess.PIPE)
        dst = subprocess.run(["ssh", RUN_HOSTS[h], f"mkdir -p {ROOT}/bin && tar -C {ROOT}/bin -xf -"], stdin=src.stdout)
        src.stdout.close()
        if src.wait() or dst.returncode:
            sys.exit(f"bs2: bin: from {frm} to {h} failed")
        print(f"{h}: {ROOT}/bin as {frm}'s")


def corpus_cases():
    """[(file, case name, source)] of cases/, by file name: the name its tier 1 row will
    have (case.name_of(), as bs2-host tier1 names it)."""
    out = []
    for f in sorted(f for f in os.listdir(f"{HERE}/cases") if f.endswith(".case")):
        with open(f"{HERE}/cases/{f}") as fh:
            c = json.load(fh)
        out.append((f, C.name_of(c), C.source_name(c)))
    return out


def corpus(plan, tier, stamp=None, have=None, only=None):
    """The corpus (cases/, or ONLY's files of it) at TIER, as run STAMP (default
    corpus-YYYYMMDD-HHMM), each case on its source's host (assign(): with HAVE, held()'s,
    over the run's hosts; else HOME's, or with --hosts held()'s), one after another."""
    cases = [f for f, _, _ in corpus_cases() if only is None or f in only]
    if plan:
        print(f"{len(cases)} corpus cases at tier {tier}")
        return
    srcs = {f: src for f, _, src in corpus_cases() if f in cases}
    ss = sorted(set(srcs.values()))
    where = (assign(ss, hosts=list(RUN_HOSTS), have=have) if have is not None else
             assign(ss, have=held(ss) if CHOSEN else None))
    sync(sorted(set(where.values())))
    by = {}
    for f in cases:
        by.setdefault(where[srcs[f]], []).append(f"{HOST_WT}/testvm/backshot2/cases/{f}")
    stamp = stamp or time.strftime("corpus-%Y%m%d-%H%M")
    for h, fs in by.items():
        if tier == 0:
            ssh(h, root(f"{HOST_BS2} tier0-cases {' '.join(fs)} --run {stamp}"))
        else:
            for f in fs:
                ssh(h, f"cd ~/backotter-work && {reserve_tier1(f)} --tier {tier} --run {stamp} --port 2949", check=False)


def leftovers_start(h, name, run):
    """The leftovers set NAME on H as RUN, detached (bs2-host leftovers: its rows in
    RUN/leftovers.jsonl, its log in logs/RUN.log), with PASS_VARS (reuse_env(): the
    bko-holt under test, the reuse switches, the word) as every other case has them."""
    log = f"/bkoscratch/backshot2/logs/{run}.log"
    ssh(h, f"mkdir -p /bkoscratch/backshot2/logs && cd ~/backotter-work && {reuse_env()}PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 setsid -f "
           f"{HOST_BS2} leftovers {name} --run {run} --port 2949 > {log} 2>&1 < /dev/null")
    print(f"{h}: started the {name} set as {run} (log {log}; rows /bkoscratch/backshot2/runs/{run}/leftovers.jsonl)")


def assign(sources, hosts=None, have=None):
    """{source: host}, one host a source (replay, shrink, soak, the corpus): its HOME host
    while that host has no more than its share (len(sources) / len(hosts), rounded up), else
    the host with the fewest sources so far (hosts' order on a tie); HAVE ({host: sources
    there}, None: all) limits each source to the hosts that have it, and the sources on the
    fewest hosts are placed first.  A source no host has: sys.exit.  Without --hosts (and
    no HOSTS given): HOME's host, the first lead host for a source it doesn't name."""
    if hosts is None and not CHOSEN:
        return {s: HOME.get(s, LEAD_HOSTS[0]) for s in sources}
    hosts = list(hosts or RUN_HOSTS)
    share = -(-len(sources) // len(hosts))
    load, out = {h: 0 for h in hosts}, {}
    can = {s: [h for h in hosts if have is None or s in have.get(h, ())] for s in sources}
    for s in sources:
        if not can[s]:
            sys.exit(f"bs2: no host of {', '.join(hosts)} has vms/{s}")
    for n in sorted({len(c) for c in can.values()}):   # the sources on the fewest hosts first
        group = [s for s in sources if len(can[s]) == n]
        for s in group:   # at home, while it has room
            h = HOME.get(s)
            if h in can[s] and load[h] < share:
                out[s] = h
                load[h] += 1
        for s in group:   # else the least loaded
            if s not in out:
                h = min(can[s], key=lambda x: (load[x], hosts.index(x)))
                out[s] = h
                load[h] += 1
    return {s: out[s] for s in sources}


# ---- BackShot2All (docs/design/bs2-all.md; bs2lib/allrun.py) ------------------------------

RUN_NAME = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*")
LEFTOVERS_SET = "leftovers"


def held_briefly(sources):
    """held(SOURCES), with its "left out for SOURCE" lines (one a host and source: ~100 for
    All) put as one line a host: the sources its cmp-run.sh --ceiling can't hold."""
    import contextlib
    import io
    err = io.StringIO()
    with contextlib.redirect_stderr(err):
        have = held(sources)
    left = {}
    for line in err.getvalue().splitlines():
        m = re.match(r"bs2: (\S+) has vms/(\S+), but ", line)
        if m:
            left.setdefault(m.group(1), []).append(m.group(2))
        else:
            print(line, file=sys.stderr)
    for h, ss in left.items():
        c = CEILINGS.get(h)
        print(f"bs2: {h} left out for {len(ss)} sources over its cmp-run.sh --ceiling"
              f"{f' ({c[0]:g} {c[1]:g})' if c else ''} (bs2lib/room.py need()): {', '.join(ss)}", file=sys.stderr)
    return have


def all_layout(have):
    """(the sources an All run runs: every built one, SOURCES' order, that a host of the run
    holds (HAVE: held()'s); {source: why} of the built ones none holds; the SKIPPED list:
    sources.py's skipped ones by piece, those, and tier 3)."""
    missing = {s: missing_why(s) for s in SOURCES if not any(s in have.get(h, ()) for h in RUN_HOSTS)}
    run = [s for s in SOURCES if s not in missing]
    return run, missing, AR.skipped(SRC.table(), missing)


def all_counts(run):
    """{source: tier 1 cases} of an All run of RUN (allrun.counts(): 200 an Alpine source,
    20 the rest); its tier 0 is COUNTS["sweep"] (main(): 1,000 unless --sweep) and tier 2
    tier2_of()'s."""
    return {s: c[1] for s, c in AR.counts(run, tier2_of, ALPINE_SOURCES).items()}


def all_later(have):
    """What an All run runs once its queues finish: (the corpus cases [(file, name, source)]
    whose source a host of the run holds; the ones left out, {name: why}; the leftovers
    set's host, the first lead host (then the rest of the run's) that holds its sources, or
    None; its steps)."""
    from bs2lib import leftovers as LO
    cs = corpus_cases()
    ok = [c for c in cs if any(c[2] in have.get(h, ()) for h in RUN_HOSTS)]
    out = {c[1]: f"its source {c[2]} is on no host of the run" for c in cs if c not in ok}
    need = set(LO.sources(LEFTOVERS_SET))
    order = [h for h in LEAD_HOSTS if h in RUN_HOSTS] + [h for h in RUN_HOSTS if h not in LEAD_HOSTS]
    host = next((h for h in order if need <= set(have.get(h, ()))), None)
    return ok, out, host, len(LO.steps(LEFTOVERS_SET))


def all_then(run):
    """The commands an All run leaves to run once its queues finish (bs2 runs the corpus in
    series from the Mac and the leftovers set detached on one host, both at port 2949: one
    after the other)."""
    hs = f" --hosts {','.join(RUN_HOSTS)}" if CHOSEN else ""
    return [f"then, once every queue is done (bs2 BackShot2All report {run} says when none is left), one after the other:",
            f"  bs2 BackShot2All corpus {run}{hs}",
            f"  bs2 BackShot2All leftovers {run}{hs}",
            f"  bs2 BackShot2All report {run}"]


def all_plan():
    """BackShot2All's plan: every source's lead, counts, seconds, room and hosts and each
    host's share (plan_words()), then the corpus and the leftovers set, the SKIPPED list by
    piece, the wall clock in all, and the verdict the run gives at best.  Reads the hosts
    (held()'s ls and cmp-run.sh --ceiling) and runs nothing."""
    from bs2lib import leftovers as LO
    have = held_briefly(SOURCES)
    run, missing, sk = all_layout(have)
    if not run:
        sys.exit("bs2: BackShot2All: no host of the run holds any built source:\n  " +
                 "\n  ".join(f"{s}: {w}" for s, w in missing.items()))
    n = all_counts(run)
    print(f"BackShot2All: {len(run)} sources, fresh (the ledger's rows excuse no case): tier 0 {sweep_n(n, run[0])} a "
          f"source, tier 1 {AR.T1_ALPINE} an Alpine source and {AR.T1} the rest, tier 2 {TIER2} Alpine's in all and "
          f"{TIER2_EACH} a UEFI source")
    longest = plan_words(run, n, have)
    space_plan(run, n, have)
    cs, out, lo_host, steps = all_later(have)
    c_s = sum(secs(src, 1) for _, _, src in cs)
    lo_s = steps * AR.LEFTOVERS_STEP_S if lo_host else 0
    print(f"then the corpus: {len(cs)} cases at tier 1, one after another on their sources' hosts, ~{c_s / 60:.0f} min est."
          + (f" (left out: {'; '.join(f'{k}: {v}' for k, v in out.items())})" if out else ""))
    print(f"then the leftovers set: {steps} steps on one disk on {lo_host}, one after another, ~{lo_s / 60:.0f} min est."
          if lo_host else f"the leftovers set: SKIPPED (no host of the run holds all of "
                          f"{', '.join(LO.sources(LEFTOVERS_SET))})")
    for line in AR.skipped_words(sk):
        print(line)
    print(f"in all: ~{(longest + c_s + lo_s) / 3600:.1f} h est. (the queues ~{longest / 3600:.1f} h, then the corpus "
          f"and the leftovers set one after the other: both take port 2949)")
    for line in all_then("RUN")[1:]:
        print(f"  (later) {line.strip()}")
    print(f"verdict: {AR.best(sk)}")


def all_start():
    """Starts a BackShot2All run, bs2all-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS: its manifest (bs2all.json: what it
    planned and SKIPPED) on each of its hosts, then run_words(); prints what is left to run
    once its queues finish (all_then())."""
    have = held_briefly(SOURCES)
    run, missing, sk = all_layout(have)
    if not run:
        sys.exit("bs2: BackShot2All: no host of the run holds any built source")
    n = all_counts(run)
    name = time.strftime("bs2all-%Y%m%d-%H%M%S")   # (seconds: two starts a minute never share a name)
    cs, out, lo_host, steps = all_later(have)
    if not lo_host:
        sk = sk + [{"name": "leftovers", "piece": "missing", "why": "no host of the run holds the set's sources"}]
    manifest = {"run": name, "word": AR.WORD, "started": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime()),
                "planned": {s: [sweep_n(n, s), n_of(n, s), tier2_of(s, run)] for s in run}, "skipped": sk,
                "corpus": [nm for _, nm, _ in cs], "corpus_out": out,
                "leftovers": {"set": LEFTOVERS_SET, "steps": steps if lo_host else 0, "host": lo_host}}
    print(f"BackShot2All {name}: {len(run)} sources; {AR.best(sk)}")
    try:
        run_words(run, n, name, have, manifest)
    finally:
        print("\n".join(all_then(name)))


def write_manifest(m, hosts, run):
    """M as ROOT/runs/RUN/bs2all.json on each of HOSTS (one line of JSON), RUN made anew:
    a host where RUN is there already (another run's) keeps it.  Every host is tried; then,
    if any failed, sys.exit naming each (no host has started anything yet)."""
    rd = f"{ROOT}/runs/{run}"
    bad = []
    for h in hosts:
        r = ssh(h, f'if [ -e {rd} ]; then echo "{rd} is there already"; exit 3; fi; '
                   f"mkdir -p {ROOT}/runs && mkdir {rd} && cat > {rd}/bs2all.json",
                check=False, capture=True, input=json.dumps(m) + "\n")
        if r.returncode:
            bad.append(f"{h}: exit {r.returncode}: {((r.stdout or '') + (r.stderr or '')).strip()[-200:]}")
    if bad:
        sys.exit(f"bs2: run {run}: not started, its manifest ({rd}/bs2all.json) not written on {len(bad)} of "
                 f"{len(hosts)} hosts:\n  " + "\n  ".join(bad))


def read_manifest(run):
    """RUN's bs2all.json from the first host of RUN_HOSTS that has it; with no --hosts,
    RUN_HOSTS becomes the run's hosts (and the leftovers set's).  Not there: sys.exit."""
    got = par({h: f"cat {ROOT}/runs/{run}/bs2all.json 2>/dev/null" for h in RUN_HOSTS})
    for h, (rc, out, _) in got.items():
        try:
            m = json.loads(out)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        if not CHOSEN:
            hs = list(m.get("hosts") or []) + [x for x in [(m.get("leftovers") or {}).get("host")] if x]
            use_hosts(",".join(dict.fromkeys(hs)) or "all")
        return m
    sys.exit(f"bs2: {run}: not a BackShot2All run (no {ROOT}/runs/{run}/bs2all.json on {', '.join(RUN_HOSTS)})")


def all_corpus(run):
    """The corpus of the All run RUN: its cases (the manifest's) at tier 1 as RUN-corpus,
    each on a host of the run that holds its source, one after another."""
    m = read_manifest(run)
    want = set(m.get("corpus") or [])
    cs = [c for c in corpus_cases() if c[1] in want]
    have = held(sorted({c[2] for c in cs}))
    ok = [c for c in cs if any(c[2] in have.get(h, ()) for h in RUN_HOSTS)]
    for c in cs:
        if c not in ok:
            print(f"bs2: corpus: {c[1]}: no host of {', '.join(RUN_HOSTS)} holds {c[2]} now: no row (the report: INCOMPLETE)",
                  file=sys.stderr)
    if ok:
        corpus(False, 1, stamp=f"{run}-corpus", have=have, only={c[0] for c in ok})
    print(f"corpus: {len(ok)} cases as {run}-corpus: bs2 BackShot2All report {run}")


def all_leftovers(run):
    """The leftovers set of the All run RUN, as RUN-lo on the manifest's host, detached."""
    m = read_manifest(run)
    h = (m.get("leftovers") or {}).get("host")
    if not h:
        sys.exit(f"bs2: {run}: its plan has no host for the leftovers set (SKIPPED)")
    if h not in RUN_HOSTS:
        sys.exit(f"bs2: {run}: the leftovers set's host {h} isn't in --hosts")
    sync([h])
    leftovers_start(h, m["leftovers"].get("set") or LEFTOVERS_SET, f"{run}-lo")


def gather_cmd(run):
    """The one command that prints a host's files of RUN, each after an "@file NAME" line,
    then (after "@file /plan", allrun.PLAN) the lead's pick lists and sweeps' plans, grep -H's
    lines (allrun.drawn_of())."""
    return ("; ".join(f'echo "@file {f}"; cat {ROOT}/runs/{run}{f} 2>/dev/null' for f in AR.FILES) +
            f'; echo "@file {AR.PLAN}"; ( cd {ROOT}/runs && grep -H . {run}/pick-*-t[12].txt {run}-t0/sweep-*.txt )'
            " 2>/dev/null; true")


def all_report(run, as_json=False):
    """The All run RUN's report (allrun.summary()): every host's rows of RUN, its sweeps
    (RUN-t0), its corpus (RUN-corpus) and its leftovers set (RUN-lo), against what its
    manifest planned; printed (with AS_JSON, as JSON).  Exit 0 for PASS or PARTIAL PASS, 1
    for FAIL or INCOMPLETE."""
    m = read_manifest(run)
    got = par({h: gather_cmd(run) for h in RUN_HOSTS})
    rows, queued, crows, lrows, lt0, unread, plan = [], [], [], [], [], [], []
    for h, (rc, out, err) in got.items():
        if rc:
            unread.append(f"{h} didn't answer ({err.strip()[-120:]}): its rows aren't counted")
            continue
        f = AR.parse_files(out)
        rows += [dict(r, host=h) for k in AR.ROW_FILES for r in f.get(k, [])]
        queued += f.get("/queue.txt", [])
        crows += [dict(r, host=h) for r in f.get("-corpus/tier1.jsonl", [])]
        lrows += [dict(r, host=h) for r in f.get("-lo/leftovers.jsonl", [])]
        lt0 += [dict(r, host=h) for r in f.get("-lo-t0/tier0.jsonl", [])]
        plan += f.get(AR.PLAN, [])
    sm = AR.summary(m, rows, queued, crows, lrows, unread, lt0, AR.drawn_of(plan))
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps(sm, indent=1))
    else:
        print("\n".join(AR.words(sm)))
    return 0 if sm["verdict"] in ("PASS", "PARTIAL PASS") else 1


def main():
    a = sys.argv[1:]
    if "--hosts" in a:
        i = a.index("--hosts")
        if i + 1 >= len(a):
            sys.exit("bs2: --hosts H,H or all")
        use_hosts(a[i + 1])
        del a[i:i + 2]
    if not a:
        sys.exit(__doc__)
    plan = "plan" in a
    a = [x for x in a if x != "plan"]
    for flag, key in (("--sweep", "sweep"), ("--tier2", "tier2")):
        if flag in a:
            i = a.index(flag)
            if i + 1 >= len(a) or not a[i + 1].isdigit():
                sys.exit(f"bs2: {flag} N")
            COUNTS[key] = int(a[i + 1])
            del a[i:i + 2]
    as_json = "--json" in a
    a = [x for x in a if x != "--json"]
    tier = 0
    if "--tier" in a:
        i = a.index("--tier")
        tier = int(a[i + 1])
        del a[i:i + 2]
    w = a[0]
    if w == "sync":
        sync()
    elif w == "status":
        status(a[1])
    elif w == "bin":
        if len(a) < 2:
            sys.exit("bs2: bin FROM")
        bin_words(a[1])
    elif w in ("BackShot2Alpine", "BackShot2"):
        os.environ["BS2_WORD"] = w   # (its cases' ledger rows' word: PASS_VARS)
        rest = a[1:]
        if rest[:1] == ["corpus"]:
            return corpus(plan, tier)
        n = int(rest[-1]) if rest and rest[-1].isdigit() else 200
        sources = [x for x in rest if not x.isdigit()] or ALPINE
        bad = [s for s in sources if s not in HOME]
        if bad:
            sys.exit("bs2: not a BackShot2 source now:\n  " + "\n  ".join(SRC.classify(s).phrase() for s in bad) +
                     f"\n(its {len(SOURCES)} sources: {', '.join(SOURCES)})")
        if plan:
            have = held(sources)
            longest = plan_words(sources, n, have)
            space_plan(sources, n, have)
            return longest
        run_words(sources, n, time.strftime("bs2a-%Y%m%d-%H%M"))
        print("then: bs2 BackShot2 corpus (once the queues finish; bs2 status RUN shows them)")
    elif w == "BackShot2All":
        # Decision 5's sizes are BackShot2All's (docs/design/bs2-all.md): its verdict says
        # every built source ran them, so --sweep and --tier2 are refused, never a smaller
        # run's PASS; BackShot2 SOURCE... takes them.
        given = [f for f in ("--sweep", "--tier2") if COUNTS.get(f[2:]) is not None]
        if given:
            sys.exit(f"bs2: BackShot2All runs decision 5's sizes ({AR.T0} tier 0, {AR.T1} tier 1 and {TIER2_EACH} tier 2 "
                     f"a source; docs/design/bs2-all.md): {' and '.join(given)} refused (smaller runs: bs2 BackShot2 "
                     f"SOURCE... N --sweep N --tier2 N)")
        os.environ["BS2_WORD"] = w   # (its cases' ledger rows' word: PASS_VARS)
        COUNTS["sweep"] = AR.T0
        rest = a[1:]
        if rest[:1] and rest[0] in ("corpus", "leftovers", "report"):
            if len(rest) != 2 or not RUN_NAME.fullmatch(rest[1]):
                sys.exit(f"bs2: BackShot2All {rest[0]} RUN (a run's name, bs2all-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS)")
            if rest[0] == "report":
                sys.exit(all_report(rest[1], as_json))
            return all_corpus(rest[1]) if rest[0] == "corpus" else all_leftovers(rest[1])
        if rest:
            sys.exit(__doc__)
        return all_plan() if plan else all_start()
    elif w == "leftovers":
        name = a[1] if len(a) > 1 else "leftovers"
        h = next(iter(RUN_HOSTS)) if CHOSEN else LEAD_HOSTS[0]
        sync([h])
        run = time.strftime("lo-%Y%m%d-%H%M")
        if plan:
            ssh(h, f"cd ~/backotter-work && {HOST_BS2} leftovers {name} --plan --run {run}-plan")
            return
        leftovers_start(h, name, run)
    elif w in ("replay", "shrink", "soak"):
        path = a[1]
        with open(path) as f:
            c = json.load(f)
        src = c["source"].split("@")[0]
        h = assign([src], have=held([src]) if CHOSEN else None)[src]
        rp = f"{HOST_WT}/testvm/backshot2/{os.path.relpath(os.path.abspath(path), HERE)}"
        stamp = time.strftime(f"{w}-%Y%m%d-%H%M")
        if plan:
            n = int(a[2]) if w == "soak" else 1
            print(f"{w} {path} on {h}: tier {tier or 1 if w == 'soak' else tier}, ~{n * secs(src, tier or 1) / 60:.0f} min est.")
            return
        sync([h])
        if w == "replay" and tier == 0:
            ssh(h, root(f"{HOST_BS2} tier0-cases {rp} --run {stamp}"))
        elif w == "replay":
            ssh(h, f"cd ~/backotter-work && {reserve_tier1(rp)} --tier {tier} --run {stamp} --port 2949", check=False)
        elif w == "shrink":
            if tier == 0:
                ssh(h, root(f"{HOST_BS2} shrink {rp} --tier 0"))
            else:
                ssh(h, f"cd ~/backotter-work && {HOST_BS2} shrink {rp} --tier {tier}")
        else:
            n = int(a[2])
            ok = 0
            for i in range(n):
                r = ssh(h, f"cd ~/backotter-work && {reserve_tier1(rp)} --tier 1 --run {stamp} --port 2949", check=False)
                ok += r.returncode == 0
            print(f"soak: {ok} of {n} passed (N of {n} bounds a race below ~{300 // max(1, n)}% only)")
    else:
        sys.exit(__doc__)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
